# Rotate-lowering mutants of candidate S1 (aien-dev/om2/compiler-s1 @ a5927895, omc 31342447...f049f).
# Run with OMC = the S1 omc born from that commit; first copy that commit's seed/omc/omc.om to
# build/om2-qual/cand-s1/omc.om (sha256 recorded in candidates/s1/RESULTS.txt). Each block: subst into a scratch
# copy, cc (built by the S1 omc), a control (OM-1 SHA abc and a rotate-free OM-2 run must still
# pass), the kill rows of sec/s3s4/mutant-kills.cases, cc pinned. The first block rebuilds the
# unmutated source: its printed sha256 must equal 3134244727189883d317e6813b93d2f55b24f2ca5e236daf6d39ef48412f049f.
cc build/om2-qual/cand-s1/omc.om
ctl-s1-rebuilt-sha run seed/qualification/om2/baseline/sha256-main.om+om/sha256/sha256.om file:seed/qualification/om2/fixtures/msg/abc.bin line:ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad - 0
correct-rot-values run seed/qualification/om2/sec/s3s4/rot-values.om+seed/qualification/om2/sec/s3s4/lib-pu.om - file:seed/qualification/om2/oracle/s3s4/exp/rot-values.out - 0
cc pinned
